Body:
After reading through the source, the GUI infrastructure for custom commands appears to already be implemented:

- `bootstrap.ts` calls `sdk.command.list()` at startup, which populates `sync.data.command`
- `prompt-input.tsx` builds the slash popover from `sync.data.command` alongside builtins
- The server-side `Command.Service` (`packages/opencode/src/command/index.ts`) loads both inline `command:` entries from config and file-based `.md` commands from all config directories (including `~/.config/opencode/command/` and `~/.opencode/command/`) via `ConfigCommand.load(dir)`
- The `SlashCommand` type already has `source: "command" | "mcp" | "skill"` and the popover renders a badge for custom commands

So the question may be whether the issue is a timing/initialization problem (commands not yet loaded when `bootstrap.ts` calls `list()`) rather than a missing implementation.

**Workaround in the meantime:** Inline `command:` entries in `opencode.json` using `{file:path}` interpolation are the most portable approach and sidestep any directory-scan timing issues:

```json
{
  "command": {
    "my-command": {
      "description": "Does something useful",
      "prompt": "{file:~/.opencode/command/my-command.md}"
    }
  }
}
```

This works in both TUI and GUI today because the config is loaded before the command service initializes, so the template is available immediately when `command.list()` is called. File-based `.md` commands in `.opencode/command/` also work but depend on `InstanceState` being fully initialized first.
